The diagnostic confirms canonical-string checking is cheap; the nested quotient summary was the bottleneck. I’m replacing it with a symbolic decimal-digit parameterization: five digit variables construct exactly every integer in `0..10000`, and the postcondition compares the binary decode to their sum. This is a full-domain theorem, not a fixed-size sample—the finite domain is represented symbolically and its coverage will also be exhaustively checked.
