codex
The single 37-element list is proving inefficient because every string is evaluated before the symbolic index is split. I’ve identified a semantics-preserving optimization: partition the table into five ranges of at most eight values, so each path evaluates only its relevant small table. If the current run does not finish shortly, I’ll apply that implementation-level change and restart from the fixed semantics.
