codex
The second long run confirms the dominant cost is the prover repeatedly deriving decimal quotient/remainder facts from the digit parameterization. I’m stopping it and making those facts explicit as redundant preconditions, accompanied by a separate machine-checked arithmetic claim showing they follow from the digit bounds. This preserves the exact input domain while giving symbolic execution the equalities it needs.
