Both bridge-free universal connection claims passed together with `#Top`: for any continuation and any integer tail `Q`, MPY’s fixed `% 10` returns the head digit and fixed `// 10` returns the tail when the number is `D + 10*Q` and `0 ≤ D < 10`. I can now use exactly those two guarded arithmetic accelerators in the main proof, with no program-defined execution skipped.
